{"type":"data","nodes":[null,{"type":"data","data":[{"mission":1,"hero":491},{"id":2,"agency":3,"agency_full":4,"sector":5,"dest":6,"color":7,"year":8,"status":9,"departure_date":10,"arrival_date":11,"transit_days":12,"vehicle":13,"payload":14,"delta_v":15,"data_quality":16,"credit":17,"links":18,"flight_data_quality":49,"fleet_refs":50,"flight":53,"name":478,"type":479,"first":480,"dispatch":481,"description":482,"events":483,"vehicle_stage":476,"flight_events":487},"voyager-2","NASA","National Aeronautics and Space Administration / Jet Propulsion Laboratory","gov","NEPTUNE","#0B3D91",1977,"FLOWN","1977-08-20","1989-08-25",4388,"Titan IIIE / Centaur","Planetair voorbijvlucht-ruimtevaartuig; elektrisch vermogen van RTG's","~18 km/s (bij benadering)","partial","© NASA / JPL-Caltech — U.S. Government work, public domain. Catalogue uses Neptune as primary destination; the mission also flew Jupiter, Saturn, and Uranus (gravity assists — not modelled in Orrery porkchops).",[19,23,27,30,34,37,40,43,46],{"l":20,"u":21,"t":22},"Voyager 2 — Wikipedia","https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Voyager_2","intro",{"l":24,"u":25,"t":26},"Voyager mission status (NASA)","https://science.nasa.gov/mission/voyager/","core",{"l":28,"u":29,"t":26},"Voyager at JPL","https://www.jpl.nasa.gov/missions/voyager-2/",{"l":31,"u":32,"t":33},"NSSDCA catalog — Voyager 2 (1977-076A)","https://nssdc.gsfc.nasa.gov/nmc/spacecraft/display.action?id=1977-076A","deep",{"l":35,"u":36,"t":33},"Neptune encounter — Smith et al. 1989, Science 246","https://www.science.org/doi/10.1126/science.246.4936.1422",{"l":38,"u":39,"t":33},"Uranus encounter — Smith et al. 1986, Science 233","https://www.science.org/doi/10.1126/science.233.4759.43",{"l":41,"u":42,"t":33},"Heliopause crossing 2018-11-05 — Krimigis et al. 2019, Nature Astronomy 3","https://www.nature.com/articles/s41550-019-0927-4",{"l":44,"u":45,"t":33},"Voyager Golden Record contents","https://voyager.jpl.nasa.gov/golden-record/whats-on-the-record/",{"l":47,"u":48,"t":33},"Voyager Interstellar Mission — current position dashboard","https://voyager.jpl.nasa.gov/mission/status/","sparse",[51],{"id":2,"role":52},"spacecraft",{"events":54,"interplanetary_profile":81,"launch":475},[55,61,67,72,77],{"met_days":56,"type":57,"label":58,"description":59,"label_en":60},0,"launch","LANCERING","Titan IIIE lanceert Voyager 2 vanaf Cape Canaveral op een Grand Tour-traject.","Launch — Titan IIIE / Centaur",{"met_days":62,"type":63,"label":64,"description":65,"label_en":66},688,"flyby","Jupiter — zwaartekrachtassist","Dichtste nadering 721.670 km op 1979-07-09. Ontdekt het gladde waterijsoppervlak van Europa en maakt de eerste gedetailleerde beelden van de lichte en donkere gebieden op Ganymedes; bevestigt de vulkaanwaarnemingen van Voyager 1 op Io. De zwaartekracht van Jupiter buigt het traject naar buiten af, richting Saturnus, dat 26 maanden later wordt bereikt — de eerste van drie planetaire assists van de missie.","Jupiter — gravity assist",{"met_days":68,"type":63,"label":69,"description":70,"label_en":71},1467,"Saturnus — zwaartekrachtassist","Dichtste nadering 101.000 km op 1981-08-26. Levert de meest gedetailleerde beelden van de ringen van Saturnus tot dan toe (spaken, gevlochten F-ring) en toont de grote lijnen van de chaotische rotatie van Hyperion. De geometrie van de ontmoeting moest door de smalle doorgang tussen Uranus en het diepe zuiden van de ecliptica — de enige route waarop beide ijsreuzen bereikbaar bleven.","Saturn — gravity assist",{"met_days":73,"type":63,"label":74,"description":75,"label_en":76},3079,"Uranus — zwaartekrachtassist","Dichtste nadering 81.500 km op 1986-01-24 — tot nu toe het enige bezoek van een ruimtesonde aan Uranus. Onthult de extreme ashelling van 98°, 10 nieuwe manen en een scheefstaand magnetisch veld. Voyager 2 kruist het ringvlak met 14,5 km/s; de katapult moet het traject daarna ongeveer 50° afbuigen om Neptunus drie jaar later te bereiken.","Uranus — gravity assist",{"met_days":12,"type"